REQUIRED UX BEHAVIOR

The fullscreen viewer must never show a blank black screen with a spinner for several seconds/minutes.

Use a progressive presentation:

Step 1

Immediately show the available thumbnail/preview image.

It is allowed to be temporary.

Do NOT show only a spinner on black if a thumbnail already exists.

Step 2

Load/resolve the original full-resolution source asynchronously.

Step 3

When the original is ready, seamlessly replace the temporary preview with the full-resolution image.

So the user sees:

tap image
→ immediate visible preview
→ full-resolution upgrade moments later.

Not:

tap image
→ black screen + spinner for an unknown amount of time.

⸻

TIMEOUT / ERROR FALLBACK

The loader must have a real failure state.

Never allow indefinite loading.

If the original full-resolution source cannot be obtained or decoded within a reasonable time:

* stop the spinner;
* keep displaying the best available preview;
* log/report the failure;
* allow retry if appropriate.

Do not freeze the user in a permanent loading state.

⸻

IMPORTANT

